Editor Feature

 
 
Symbol	Element	What it is
📝 Text	Text box	Words you type on the slide
🔷 Shape	Shape	Rectangles, circles, arrows, lines, stars, etc.
🖼️ Image	Image	A photo or picture you upload or pick
🎞️ GIF	Giphy / GIF	A moving picture from the GIPHY search
⭐ Icon	Icon	A small symbol (from Lucide, Phosphor, Material libraries)
🔗 Embed	Embed	A YouTube/Vimeo/Loom video, a link card, or a Mermaid diagram
 
Good to know: The editor also has Charts and Tables, but you
didn't ask about those, so they are left out of the element tables. They are
mentioned only where a common action (like delete or layering) works on them too.
 
Good to know about GIFs: A GIF is treated as a special kind of image.
So a GIF can do everything an image can do (crop, filter, border, shadow,
flip, rotate…). The only things unique to GIFs are how you find and add them
(the GIPHY search). That's why the GIF column mostly mirrors the Image column.
 

 
TABLE 1 — Common features (work across many elements)
These are the everyday actions: select, move, resize, rotate, layer, copy, etc.
 
Feature	What it does (plain English)	📝 Text	🔷 Shape	🖼️ Image	🎞️ GIF	⭐ Icon	🔗 Embed
Select	Click once to pick an element	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Multi-select (Shift+Click)	Hold Shift and click to pick several at once	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Multi-select (drag a box)	Drag a rectangle over empty canvas to grab everything inside	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Select all (Ctrl/Cmd+A)	Pick every unlocked element on the slide	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Move / drag	Drag to reposition	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Nudge with arrow keys	Tap arrows to move 1px (Shift+arrow = 10px)	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Resize (corner handles)	Drag a corner to scale	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Resize (edge handles)	Drag a side to stretch width or height	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Keep proportions (Shift while resizing)	Hold Shift so it doesn't distort	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Rotate	Drag the round handle to spin it	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Bring to front	Put on top of everything	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Send to back	Put behind everything	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Bring forward (1 step)	Move up one layer	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Send backward (1 step)	Move down one layer	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Group / Ungroup	Lock several together so they move as one	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Copy / Cut / Paste	Standard clipboard actions	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Duplicate	Make an instant copy (+20px offset)	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Duplicate to other slides	Copy onto this / selected / all slides	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Delete	Remove from slide	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Undo / Redo	Step back / forward through changes	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Lock / Unlock	Freeze so it can't be moved by accident	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Opacity	Make see-through (0–100%)	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Align (left/center/right/top/middle/bottom)	Line up 2+ elements	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Distribute (even spacing)	Space 3+ elements evenly	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Right-click menu	Context menu of actions	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Exact position (X / Y)	Type precise coordinates	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Exact size (W / H)	Type precise width / height	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
Hyperlink	Make it clickable (URL / email / jump to slide)	✅	✅*	✅	✅		—
Copy-style / Alt+drag clone	Hold Alt and drag to duplicate in one move	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅	✅
 
* Shapes carry links via their inner text.
— Embed already is a link/video, so a separate hyperlink isn't offered.
 

 
TABLE 2 — Text-only features
Things you can only do to a text box.
 
Feature	What it does
Font family	Pick the typeface (built-in or your own uploaded font)
Font size	1–900px
Bold / Italic / Underline / Strikethrough	The four classic styles
Text color	Color of the letters
Highlight color	Colored background behind selected words
Text alignment	Left / center / right / justify
Line height	Space between lines
Letter spacing	Space between letters
Paragraph spacing (before / after)	Space above and below paragraphs
Bullet list	Dotted list
Numbered list	1, 2, 3 list
List indent / outdent	Nest list items deeper or shallower
Text case	UPPERCASE / lowercase / Capitalize
Link	URL, email, jump-to-slide, or embed
Text type preset	One-click Title / H1–H5 / Paragraph styles (sets size, weight, etc.)
Aspect-ratio lock	Lock the box width/height ratio while resizing
Type-to-edit	Select a text box and just start typing to edit it
 

 
TABLE 3 — Shape-only features
Things you can only do to a shape.
 
Feature	What it does
Fill color	Solid color inside the shape
Fill gradient	Linear / radial / conic color blend
Fill image	Put a picture inside the shape (with scale, offset, fit)
Border / stroke color	Color of the outline
Border / stroke width	Thickness of the outline
Border / stroke style	Solid, dashed, dotted
Line end caps	Arrow / dot / dash ends (for line shapes)
Corner radius (all 4 corners)	Round the corners equally
Corner radius (per corner)	Round each corner separately
Geometry handles	Shape-specific adjusters (arrowhead size, star points, etc.)
Blur	Soften the shape
Shadow	Drop shadow
Text inside shape	Type rich text inside, with full text formatting
Step-connector controls	Routing / step count / mid-point for connector lines
 

 
TABLE 4 — Image-only features (the "uncommon" ones)
This is the special table you asked for — features that exist only for images
(and therefore also for GIFs, since a GIF is an image). These go beyond the basic
move/resize and are what make the image editor powerful.
 
Feature	What it does
Upload / replace	Add your own image, or swap one for another
Crop	Trim the image with drag handles
Crop ratios	Presets: free, 1:1, 4:3, 3:4, 16:9, 9:16, ellipse, circle
Focus point	Choose which part stays visible when cropped to "cover"
Object fit	cover / contain / fill / none
Filters (16 presets)	One-click looks — see the filter list below
Blur	Soften the image (0–20px)
Color overlay	Tint the image a color
Overlay opacity	How strong the tint is (0–100%, default 40%)
Overlay blend mode	8 modes: normal, multiply, screen, overlay, soft-light, hard-light, color, luminosity
Corner radius	Round the image corners (0–100px)
Standard border	Solid border with width (1–30px) + color
Special border styles (6)	Inner-shadow, thin-frame, double-frame, film, polaroid, rounded-white
Shadow	Drop shadow with angle, distance, blur, size, color, opacity
Flip horizontal	Mirror left↔right
Flip vertical	Mirror top↔bottom
Reset all styles	One click back to defaults
Alt text	Description for accessibility
Set as slide background	Make the image fill the whole slide as the backdrop
SVG recolor	For SVG images: change up to 20 individual colors
 
The 16 image filters
 
Group	Filter	The look
Monochrome	None	No filter
	Noir	Black & white, high contrast, darker
	Gray	Plain black & white
	Sepia	Old brown-tone photo
Color grading	Vintage	Faded, slightly warm
	Warm	Warm orange tint
	Cool	Cool blue tint
	Cross	Punchy, warm, high-saturation
Exposure	Bright	Lighter and punchier
	Dark	Darker, more contrast
	Faded	Light and washed-out
	Matte	Flat, muted colors
Drama	Dynamic	High contrast + saturation
	Vibrant	Extreme saturation
	Dramatic	Very high contrast, darker
	Soft	Gentle, lifted colors
 
Adjustable ranges (for the sliders)
 
Slider	Min	Max	Default	Step
Blur	0	20 px	0	0.5
Overlay opacity	0	100%	40%	1
Shadow angle	0	360°	135°	5
Shadow distance	0	200 px	8	1
Shadow blur	0	80 px	6–12	1
Shadow size	0	80 px	0	1
Shadow opacity	0	100%	25–40%	1
Border width	1	30 px	4	1
Corner radius	0	100 px	0	1
Opacity	0	100%	100%	1
 

 
TABLE 5 — Icon-only features
 
Feature	What it does
Icon library	Choose source: Lucide, Phosphor, or Material
Icon name	Pick which icon
Icon color	Recolor the icon
Icon weight (Phosphor only)	thin / light / regular / bold / fill / duotone
 

 
TABLE 6 — Embed-only features
 
Feature	What it does
Embed type	YouTube / Vimeo / Loom / Mermaid / Link
URL or video ID	Where the content comes from
Title	Caption shown on the preview
Thumbnail	Preview image (auto-fetched)
Mermaid code	For Mermaid type: the diagram source code
 

 
TABLE 7 — GIF (Giphy) features
A GIF reuses every Image feature (Table 1 + Table 4). These extras are about
finding and adding GIFs:
 
Feature	What it does
GIPHY search	Search animated GIFs by keyword
Trending GIFs	Shows popular GIFs when you open the panel
Infinite scroll	Loads more as you scroll (up to 500)
Animated on the slide	The GIF plays automatically
Original size captured	Keeps the GIF's real dimensions
"Powered by GIPHY" credit	Attribution shown in the panel
 

 
TABLE 8 — Canvas features (the workspace itself)
Not tied to one element — these are about the whole editing area.
 
Feature	What it does
Zoom in / out	25% up to 300%
Zoom presets	Jump to 25 / 50 / 75 / 100 / 200 / 300%
Fit to slide	Snap back to 100%
Grid vs. normal view	See all slides as a grid, or one at a time
Rulers (top + side)	Measurement rulers; drag from them to make guides
Smart alignment guides	Pink snap-lines while you drag (Figma-style)
Spacing guides	Shows the gap size between elements
Safe-margin guides	Dashed lines marking safe edges
Custom guides	Your own draggable reference lines
Layout grid overlay	Columns / rows / margins grid
Distance measurement	Alt-hover shows distance between two elements
Dimension tooltip	Live W×H while resizing, X:Y while dragging, R° while rotating
Slide background	Color, opacity, image, pattern, focus point, scale
 

 
TABLE 9 — Slide thumbnail panel (left side)
The strip of mini-slides down the left.
 
Feature	What it does
Thumbnail previews	Live mini-version of each slide
Grid or list view	Two ways to show the slides
Add slide	Blank, from a template, or AI-generated
Duplicate slide(s)	Clone one or many
Delete slide(s)	Remove one or many
Reorder by drag	Drag slides to reorder (single or multiple)
Select slides	Click; Shift+Click = range; Ctrl/Cmd+Click = toggle
Navigate with arrow keys	Up/Down to move between slides
Move up / down	Shift a slide's position
Hide / show slide	Skip a slide during the show
Status badge	To-Do / In-Progress / Done markers
Comment badge	Shows comment count
Animation badge	Marks slides with animations/transitions
AI badge	Marks AI-generated slides
Slide title	Auto-pulled from the first text box
AI update slide	Regenerate a slide via Gemini or Claude
Smart-diagram export	Export slide(s) as diagram steps
 

 
TABLE 10 — Layers panel
The list that shows every element stacked in order.
 
Feature	What it does
Layer list	Every element shown in stacking order
Thumbnails & type icons	Preview + a letter for the element kind
Select from list	Click a row to select on canvas (Shift+Click for many)
Group badges	"G1", "G2"… labels for grouped items
Front / back / forward / backward	Reorder stacking from the panel
Drag to reorder	Drag rows to restack (single or block)
Background image controls	Set / replace / detach / delete the background
Collapse panel	Hide / show the layer list
Element counter	"N elements" in the header
 

 
Keyboard shortcuts
 
Action	Mac	Windows
Copy	⌘C	Ctrl+C
Cut	⌘X	Ctrl+X
Paste	⌘V	Ctrl+V
Duplicate	⌘D	Ctrl+D
Undo	⌘Z	Ctrl+Z
Redo	⌘⇧Z / ⌘Y	Ctrl+Shift+Z / Ctrl+Y
Group	⌘G	Ctrl+G
Ungroup	⌘⇧G	Ctrl+Shift+G
Select all	⌘A	Ctrl+A
Delete	⌫	Del / Backspace
Bring forward	⌘]	Ctrl+]
Send backward	⌘[	Ctrl+[
Bring to front	⌘⌥]	Ctrl+Alt+]
Send to back	⌘⌥[	Ctrl+Alt+[
Bold	⌘B	Ctrl+B
Italic	⌘I	Ctrl+I
Underline	⌘U	Ctrl+U
Strikethrough	⌘⇧X	Ctrl+Shift+X
Toggle case	⌘⇧U	Ctrl+Shift+U
Save	⌘S	Ctrl+S
Nudge 1px	Arrow keys	Arrow keys
Nudge 10px	Shift+Arrow	Shift+Arrow
New text box	T	T
Deselect / cancel	Esc	Esc
 

 
